{
 "about": [
  "Which state a bot is in (PROTOCOL.md, \"What a bot is doing now\", `bots.state`): the box's rule, `botsNow`, `botState` and `botNow` in",
  "box/src/link/lists/rule.ts, which box/test/bot-states.test.ts holds to these. `counts` is what its sessions come to (`expect.bots` in",
  "session-lists.json: at work, waiting on you, thinking, blocked, and `unseen`, when the newest turn you haven't read ended); or, in its place,",
  "`sessions` (the bot's sessions' facts, as the session list says them) and `seen` (when you last saw each bot, ms, `POST kuvo/bots/<id>/seen`),",
  "which `botsNow` makes them from for `bot`: a turn that ended then or before isn't unseen, and a hard stop it ended on doesn't block (a retry",
  "under way, at work, still does). `rest` is its `paused` and next wake-up (`wakes`, seconds), `at` now (ms) and `before` what the box last said",
  "of it. `expect.now` is its `now` in `kuvo/bots`: the first state that holds of needsYou, blocked, thinking (every one at work thinks), working,",
  "done, asleep (paused, or its next wake-up more than 12 hours away) and idle, and since when (`at` for a state new since `before`, `before`'s for",
  "the same, and for done when the turn ended). `expect.turns`: when its state changes with nothing else changing (its next wake-up comes within",
  "12 hours, ms), else null. A client adds `offline` itself; it works none of this out."
 ],
